UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["COBIT eliminates the need to comply with individual regulations","COBIT is a mandatory regulatory requirement for all organizations","COBIT provides a unified governance structure that maps to multiple regulatory requirements","COBIT replaces all other security frameworks entirely"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Per COBIT 2019 Framework (Introduction and Methodology), COBIT provides a unified governance structure that maps multiple regulatory requirements (SOX, PCI DSS, GLBA) to a single framework, reducing duplication of effort. It serves as an integrating layer that harmonizes how an organization addresses diverse compliance obligations.
Wrong (A): COBIT does not eliminate the obligation to comply with individual regulations. Organizations must still satisfy each applicable regulation independently.
Wrong (B): COBIT is a voluntary governance framework, not a mandatory regulatory requirement for any organization.
