  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Per NIST SP 800-53 PS-4 (Personnel Termination) and NIST SP 800-61 Rev. 2, Section 2.3, this scenario represents a classic insider threat where a former employee retains system access due to failures in the offboarding process. Insider threats are particularly dangerous because the individual possesses legitimate knowledge of systems and data locations.
