Wrong (B): Script kiddie attacks are opportunistic and use readily available tools without specific targeting. This attack shows deliberate, sustained effort against a specific contractor.
Wrong (C): Denial of service disrupts availability through traffic flooding, not stealthy data exfiltration over months via a compromised third party.
Wrong (D): Accidental exposure involves misconfiguration, not a deliberate multi-month campaign by a sophisticated threat group.$EXPL$
