-- Q3630: Threats, Attacks, and Vulnerabilities [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Low-severity vulnerabilities never warrant remediation resources","The penetration test methodology used was fundamentally flawed","Only critical-rated vulnerabilities matter in a risk assessment","Chaining low-severity findings can escalate combined impact beyond individual ratings"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Per NIST SP 800-115 Section 7.1 and the OWASP Testing Guide, vulnerability chaining demonstrates that individually low-severity weaknesses can be combined into a significant attack path. This finding illustrates why penetration testing provides value beyond automated scanning by revealing how multiple findings interact to create critical exploitation paths.
Wrong (A): Low-severity vulnerabilities may be exploitable in combination with other weaknesses and should not be categorically dismissed from remediation.
Wrong (B): Discovering chained vulnerabilities validates the methodology. The test successfully identified a risk that automated scanning would have missed.
