-- Q3640: Threats, Attacks, and Vulnerabilities [medium/L1]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["SQL injection manipulating backend database queries","Cross-site scripting injecting malicious browser scripts","Session fixation forcing a predetermined session identifier","Directory traversal accessing files outside the intended path"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Per NIST SP 800-53 Rev. 5, control SI-10 (Information Input Validation), directory traversal exploits insufficient input validation by manipulating file path references using sequences like ../ to access files outside the application''s intended root directory. This can expose sensitive system files such as /etc/passwd and configuration files.
Wrong (A): SQL injection targets database query interpretation through unsanitized input, not the file system access layer.
Wrong (B): Cross-site scripting injects malicious scripts into web pages that execute in other users'' browsers, not file system traversal.
Wrong (C): Session fixation forces a user to authenticate with a known session ID. It does not involve accessing files outside the application directory.$EXPL$
